that woman nearly died.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.670
- This is pure nonsense.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.840
You can't know that someone
needs a cardiac transplant

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.740
after doing a quick ultrasound bedside.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.600
It's ridiculous, it's joke,

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.040
a further workup needs to be done.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.000
A proper thorough history needs to happen.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.190
You don't know why she
had that fluid there.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:08.990
So a cardiology consult is
appropriate now not then

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:10.190
when you should have scanned her heart

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:12.313
to begin with to see why it stopped.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:16.963
- Emma, Emma is this your mother's baby?

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.380
- You didn't know?

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.780
I thought I told that nurse.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:23.680
She was pregnant when my dad got sick.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.853
It was in plant, but she was so happy.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.920
And how was it?

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.860
- Well, I think your mother has,

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:31.810
what's called a postpartum cardiomyopathy.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.620
It's a rare heart
condition that can develop

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:34.453
after having a baby.

00:10:34.453 --> 00:10:36.560
- God, how do you diagnose that?

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.550
This is one of those moments
where TV and real science

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:40.610
completely collide.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.200
Should this be in the differential,

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.870
meaning the list of potential illnesses?

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:44.900
Absolutely.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.330
Should you jump and assume
that it's definitely that

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:49.520
and tell the family that
it's that before you've done

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:51.140
any confirmation tests?

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:54.550
No, it's just not in the way
we do things in hospitals,

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.670
Because if we constantly had
an idea that it was something

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.330
and we pitched it to the
patient, it was wrong,

00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.810
and then we said something
else, and it was wrong.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:01.110
Patients will lose faith in us.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:03.530
And that's why we have a list
of things that we're actively

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:04.970
trying to rule out or rule in.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.330
And sometimes it's a
combination of two things.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.460
Life is never that simple
or straightforward.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.970
Are you a fan of medical dramas?

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:11.900
What about scrubs?

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.910
I put a playlist together for you here,

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:15.920
or if you want to learn a
little bit more about me

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.730
and my personality, I
took a personality test.

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:19.750
Are they even accurate?

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:21.070
You'll find out in this video,

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:23.407
and as always stay happy and healthy

